Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Add a fips feature to linkerd-policy-controller that turns on the rustls fips feature, so
 the FIPS package variant builds against the AWS-LC FIPS module (aws-lc-fips-sys) instead of aws-lc-sys.
 The Cargo.lock hunks add the crates that the feature pulls in, with prettyplease held at 0.2.37 because
 the newer 0.3.0 does not compile against the bindgen 0.73.2 that aws-lc-fips-sys needs.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/linkerd/linkerd2.git f6415cf0f2a6e9e04aab969083907bde4be0ea20
Verify: cmd `strings /usr/bin/linkerd-policy-controller` expect "AWS-LC FIPS"
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream ships no FIPS build of the policy controller)
Drop-When: never: upstream ships no FIPS build of the policy controller
Regenerate: `printf '\n[features]\nfips = ["rustls/fips"]\n' >> policy-controller/Cargo.toml && cargo check -p linkerd-policy-controller --features fips`
Upstream: https://github.com/linkerd/linkerd2/blob/edge-26.10.1/policy-controller/Cargo.toml
--- a/policy-controller/Cargo.toml
+++ b/policy-controller/Cargo.toml
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 license = "Apache-2.0"
 publish = false
 
+[features]
+fips = ["rustls/fips"]
+
 [dependencies]
 anyhow = "1"
 tokio = { version = "1", features = ["macros", "rt", "rt-multi-thread"] }
